#####################################################################
# tri21_sq_k10001.lgi
#
# polygon  : sq_k10001.poly
# expect   : valid
# picture  : small
# big      : yes
#
# WHAT:
#   unit square, 10001 segments per side (40004 vertices).
#   Vertex spacing 1e-4: the old fixed 1e-8 tolerance classed every
#   corner as collinear, so no cell could be made at all.
#   SLOW: about 34 s with the fix (the algorithm is O(n^2)), so it
#   is SKIPPED in the normal run (user, Oct 12 2026); run it with
#       BIG=1 run_triangulate_tests.sh
#   tri32 (sq_small: spacing 1e-4 in a 0.01 square) fails the original
#   code the same way in under a second. What only this deck adds:
#   40 004 vertices and more than 9 999 cells (the old i4 cell count
#   printed ****).
#
# THE ORIGINAL CODE (before the Oct 2026 fix):
#   FAILS: "ERROR: Unable to triangulate input".
#####################################################################
cmo / create / mo_tri / / / triplane
read / avs / sq_k10001.poly / mo_tri
triangulate / counterclockwise
dump / avs / out_tri21_sq_k10001.inp / mo_tri
finish
